[align=center]
[size=200][b]Reference — Installer, Discovery, SNMP2MQTT & UniFi2MQTT[/b][/size]
[/align]
[hr]
Switch Vision is a multi-component platform. Components deliberately have independent version numbers.

[notice]Do not expect version numbers to match. Switch Vision Installer is the normal authority for installed/latest component status.[/notice]

[size=150][b]Switch Vision Installer[/b][/size]
Repository: https://github.com/zemerdon/switch-vision-installer
Handles Core installation/updates, supporting app registration, component status, dependency-aware Update All, recovery backups, validated restore operations and restart requirements.

[size=150][b]Switch Vision Discovery / Hub[/b][/size]
Discovery performs current hardware collection, exact-model detection and configuration generation.
[code]Validate → Collect → Identify → Generate telemetry → Generate dashboard → Verify handoff → Complete[/code]
[b]Switch Name (Used internally only)[/b] is the stable machine identity. [b]Display name[/b] is the friendly card title.

[size=150][b]SNMP2MQTT[/b][/size]
Authoritative Discovery-generated handoff:
[code]/share/switch_vision/generated-snmp2mqtt.yaml[/code]
Do not maintain a second active copied version of the same generated configuration.

[size=150][b]UniFi2MQTT[/b][/size]
UniFi2MQTT is optional and provides a read-only path from the official UniFi Network Integration API.
Configure it from:
[code]Switch Vision Hub → UniFi2MQTT Settings[/code]
Secret values are stored through Home Assistant Supervisor and are not read back into the browser.
Switch Vision does not fabricate missing UniFi telemetry. SNMP2MQTT can remain the source for traffic data the UniFi API does not expose suitably.

[size=150][b]Configuration ownership[/b][/size]
The Hub provides one management surface, but each component retains ownership of its authoritative settings. Partial cross-component save failures are reported rather than hidden.
